    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba809af6_75e7738c",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/geom/Rect.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 5633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-08T17:41:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I like \"Rect\" better. I think Rect is a subset of all things that could be considered \"Bounds\" and therefore more specific. I also think that the association with SkRect actually helps people already familiar with Skia understand the purpose and functionality.\n\nI actually wouldn\u0027t mind using this class on \"Shape\" and other places inside of Graphite that use rects. WDYT? I could see the fast intersection logic being useful for tightening clip bounds and draw rects, etc.",
      "parentUuid": "0ccc5acb_50330b91",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "6a3590e3bbefcccf37325279c3f0844ed88b134a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07d96d63_2f6e3dd1",
