        "id": 5633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-08T17:41:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So skvx::any() is a template function, right?\n\nI wouldn\u0027t think it possible to access them without \"skvx::\" because all these functions are defined inside the skvx namespace. (I\u0027ll double check when I write the test.)\n\nWe could add some \"using\" declarations in skgpu, but I think it\u0027s important to keep these methods explicitly inside skvx:: because min/max/sqrt/ceil/floor/etc. all have different non-vector implementations.",
      "parentUuid": "2f155a8b_a1aed440",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 64,
        "startChar": 44,
